# Every file in this repository is verified by sha256 (SHA256SUMS,
# SHA256SUMS.bundle, best_S315/SHA256SUMS, best_S315/L1pp/LEAF_INDEX.json).
# Git must therefore never rewrite line endings on checkout: with the default
# core.autocrlf=true of Git for Windows, a clone would receive CRLF and every
# recorded hash would fail to match -- the stored objects are correct, but the
# working tree would not be what was certified.
#
# "-text" disables all end-of-line conversion.  It does not change what is
# stored; it only makes every checkout byte-identical to the certified files.
* -text
